  "etymologyNotes": [
    {
      "s": "makemeahanzi",
      "t": "The leg 口 above the foot"
    },
    {
      "s": "dong_chinese",
      "t": "Pictograph of a foot attached to a leg."
    },
    {
      "s": "shuowen_jiezi",
      "t": "人之足也。在下。从止、口。凡足之屬皆从足。",
      "w": 1
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Pictogram (象形) of a leg; the pictogram is similar to ⽦. See also 𠯣, which points to the fact that 之 is the pictogram of a footprint.\nUncertain. Compare Proto-Mon-Khmer *ɟuŋ ~ *ɟuəŋ ~ *ɟəŋ (“leg, foot”), whence Mon ဇိုၚ် (cf. Schuessler, 2007)."
    },
    {
      "s": "wiktionary",
      "t": "Probably Sino-Tibetan; compare Tibetan ཆོག (chog, “to be sufficient”) (Coblin, 1986)."
    }
  ],
  "shuowen": "人之足也。在下。从止、口。凡足之屬皆从足。",
  "shuowenExplanation": "foot of man. be at; under. Ideographic compound of 止、口 \"stop\" and 足 \"foot\". All characters in the 足 \"foot\" category use this as radical.",
